# Pharmacy Inventory Management System

## Project Overview
The Pharmacy Inventory Management System is a Python-based application designed to manage pharmacy operations efficiently. It helps administrators maintain medicine records, monitor stock levels, manage suppliers, track expiry dates, and record sales and purchases.

## Key Features

- User Registration and Login
- Admin Authentication and Permissions
- Medicine Management (Add, View, Update, Delete)
- Batch Management
- Automatic Expiry Notifications
- Low Stock Alerts
- Stock Summary
- Supplier Management
- Purchase Management
- Medicine Sales and Billing
- Sales History
- Purchase History
- Inventory Reports
- Activity Log

## Technologies Used

- Python
- SQLite
- CSV

## Database
The application uses SQLite to store medicine details, batch information, supplier records, purchases, sales, and other inventory data.

## How to Run

1. Download or clone this repository.
2. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
3. Run the following command:

   python main.py

4. Follow the application menu to access the available features.

## Project Purpose
The main objective of this project is to simplify pharmacy inventory management, reduce manual work, improve stock monitoring, and help prevent losses caused by expired medicines.

